Ted,

Check out: http://eijk.homelinux.org/~stefan/slbd.html. It's the script 
I use to automatically rebuild Mandrake's distro on the alpha. The 
script uses urpmi quite a lot. To use the script on RH you'll probably 
have to port urpmi over to RH, and since RH is using a newer version 
rpm, this can be quite some work.

I don't run it in a chroot environment, but I use a dedicated & empty 
system for it. In theory the package should rebuild if basesystem + 
rpm-build + BuildRequires are installed on the system. The script 
installs the BuildRequires and attempts to rebuild. Often the 
BuildRequires are incomplete or incorrect, resulting in failed builds.

I alsa keep the build outputs online. Check out: 
http://eijk.homelinux.org/build/cooker/

Stefan van der Eijk



