 Ok I did some more R&D.

When I compile my kernels as a 164LX specific kernel, my machine does not
make it through the linux bootup process. It complains that it looses the
IRQ for my IDE Hard Drive. It also complains that it looses teh irq for
teh scsi drive but resets it succesfully. The whole process halts when the
system tries to bring up the ethernet cards. It just hangs.

BUT, when I compile the kernel as generic...everything works fine.

I have tested this with Kernel-2.4.19 and 2.4.20 and i get the same results.

Anyone have this problem as well?

John





