> teh scsi drive but resets it succesfully. The whole process halts when the
> system tries to bring up the ethernet cards. It just hangs.
> 
> BUT, when I compile the kernel as generic...everything works fine.

If you are booting from SRM, did you make sure to answer the

	"Use SRM as bootloader"

question as YES? If you answered NO (prolly the default), then the
kernel is getting confused because the PALcode is delivering interrupts
in one way, and the kernel is interpreting them in a different way.

 --Jay++

