> On Mon, Feb 10, 2003 at 08:56:04AM -0800, John Weez wrote:
>>
>> When I compile my kernels as a 164LX specific kernel, my machine does
>> not make it through the linux bootup process. It complains that it
>> looses the IRQ for my IDE Hard Drive. It also complains that it looses
>> teh irq for teh scsi drive but resets it succesfully. The whole
>> process halts when the system tries to bring up the ethernet cards. It
>> just hangs.
>>
>> BUT, when I compile the kernel as generic...everything works fine.
>
> If you are booting from SRM, did you make sure to answer the
>
> 	"Use SRM as bootloader"
>
> question as YES? If you answered NO (prolly the default), then the
> kernel is getting confused because the PALcode is delivering interrupts
> in one way, and the kernel is interpreting them in a different way.
>
>  --Jay++
