It is not futile, the gentoo distribution for the Alpha arch is working OK, if 
you take precautions and do not use -mcpu=ev6 or -mcpu=ev67 and some packages 
like openssh will not properly compile with -O2, you must add a 
-fno-sched-interblock to get it to compile properly, other apps will work 
with -O1 instead of -O2, but a few apps will require a little patching to 
make them work correctly.

I consider these bugs to be significant if you are a commercial user and need 
a rock steady system.   A home / hobby system should be doable with a little 
bit of effort.  In the worst case, I hope you give it a try and report the 
problems, as I believe that defining the issues is the first step toward 
solving them.

I hope this helps.

Best Regards,


--George

