You can probably buy ECC registered DIMM's at a good in-town shop, but it 
will cost you.  My personal recommendation is to buy from 
http://www.crucial.com .  (I have no ties to it, just good experience.)  I 
bought memory for my LX, the wrong kind, and they took it back on an 
exchange with no restocking fee (they reserve that right, but seldom do 
it.)  2nd day FedEx shipping is also free.  The memory is Micron, so it is 
quality stuff.

I bought non-ecc memory for my LX, and I called them up and they said 
"Sure, let me give you the RMA department."  In about 5 minutes, I had an 
RMA, and they cross shipped my new memory (with a credit card.)  After that 
experience, I have a very hard time buying memory from anywhere else.

Ted




