step one: acquire srpms
step two: for i in `ls -1`; do rpm --rebuild $i >$i.log 2>&1; done
step three: grep "Wrote: /usr/src/redhat/RPMS/" *.log >finished.list
step four: ls *.log >started.list
step five: find a way to parse the output of step 3. I used perl with a
	simple split and print.
step six:  cat started.list finished.list | sort | uniq -u
>unfinished.list
step seven:  grep "error: failed build dependencies" *.log | perl
logparse.pl >dependencies.log
step eight: cat unfinished.list dependencies.log | sort | uniq -u
>failed.log

So far (I admit, advanced workstation src rpms on a 7.3 i386 system) out
of 690 source rpms, I've had 480 successful compiles, 163 that failed on
dependencies to build it, and ... 47 failures

Now I just need glue to go and resolve dependencies and retry ...

-- 
-- John E. Jasen (jjasen1@umbc.edu)
