With regards to your message at 09:44 AM 2/12/03, Ted Goodridge, Jr. Where 
you stated:

>You can probably buy ECC registered DIMM's at a good in-town shop, but it 
>will cost you.  My personal recommendation is to buy from 
>http://www.crucial.com .  (I have no ties to it, just good experience.)  I 
>bought memory for my LX, the wrong kind, and they took it back on an 
>exchange with no restocking fee (they reserve that right, but seldom do 
>it.)  2nd day FedEx shipping is also free.  The memory is Micron, so it is 
>quality stuff.
Don;t count on it.
A good bit of the Crucial stuff is from other suppliers.
For example Transcend now builds a lot of their modules.

>I bought non-ecc memory for my LX, and I called them up and they said 
>"Sure, let me give you the RMA department."  In about 5 minutes, I had an 
>RMA, and they cross shipped my new memory (with a credit card.)  After 
>that experience, I have a very hard time buying memory from anywhere else.
>
>Ted


Their service and prices are good.
I did have one bad experience with them:
Back about 2 years ago when DDR was a new thing, and hard to source, they 
were the first n the market with PC1600 (200MHz) DDR
We got a bunch from them, and had quite a few fail.
They were OK about warranty returns, but the replacements failed often too.
Finally it was getting out of hand, and we asked if we could get a credit 
on some we had to return for the THIRD time, and they refused.
We did not ask for cash back, only a credit to buy something else from them.

So, not all perfect.

My recommendation:
Corsair
Kentronn

We have used RAM from both, and it works well on these boards, and I also 
know the PC2700 is advised of you are using over 2GB on it.
We HAVE tested with 4GB, and it works pretty nicely, as log as you are 
fussy about the RAM.

DO update the firmware with the file I sent, though!

It's on our ftp if anyone else needs it.


