I looked into watercooling a couple of years ago.  The big problem I see is the
bolts that the heat sink and pad are mounted on are physically part of the CPU.
There appears to be nothing like it in the x86 world.  I haven't gotten the urge
(or sanity loss) to attempt to hacksaw them off for a watercooler block.  ;-)

I think right now the loudest thing in my LX system is the CPU fan.
It's a Delta rated at 38dB.  I need the extra airflow 'cause the 533 is
overclocked to 600.  I've found that I can reduce the noise a bit by not
mounting the fan flush against the heatsink.  I got that idea from the Zalman
heatsinks that use a 80mm fan mounted a couple of inches away from the
heatsink.  Still, I'm looking around for a quieter fan with a higher CFM
rating than the stock fan that came with the system.

Alan

