Eugene Chu wrote:
> Hi Folks,
> 
> This may be a simple question that everyone already knows, but how do
> I access SCSI devices with multiple LUNs on a target ID?  I have a RAID
> with 3 LUNs (0, 1, 2) connected to an Adaptec 7899 HBA, which sees all
> 3 LUNs with the SCSI configuration utility, but I don't know how to
> address them from Linux (RH 7.2, kernel 2.4.9-32.5smp)  The LUN 0
> can be accessed as /dev/sdc, but I have been unable to get at LUNs 1
> and 2.  Is there some configuration I have to change?

The kernel has to be compiled to probe all LUNs.  After that is done it 
is a little confusing to find the devices.  If LUN 0 is /dev/sdc, LUN 1 
will usually get mapped to /dev/sdd.  I prefer devfs instead of static 
files.  devfs makes all the parts of the SCSI mapping painfully obvious 
(and if you run devfsd you'll have sym links to the obvious mappings).

