IIRC this can only be accessed by taking the card an plugging it into an
x86 machine. Although, depending on the alpha that you have, you might be
able to run the old AlphaBIOS to access the card then reboot and switch
back to SRM (for those machines that hold both images - I"m not suggesting
to flash back and forth for those machines that can only hold SRM or
ARC/AlphaBIOS). I was able to access the SCSI BIOS for a Qlogic and a
INITIO SCSI cards through the alphaBIOS.

James



