I checked with a friend at a machine shop yesterday.
I can get a copper and aluminum water block machined for around $150.
This includes a copper base plate heat spreader, 3mm thick, and this is 
bonded to an aluminum block 24mm tall, with a "U" shaped passageway, 6mm x 
6mm in cross-section. Both ends of the passageway terminating in a metal 
tube fitting, 1/4" tune size.
Includes the wells for the nuts to match the studs on the CPU.
The majority of the water cooling kits out there use either 1/4" or 3/16" 
plastic tubing.

Production time would be 1 to 2 weeks depending on how busy they are at the 
time.

Additional ones would be a bit less money, as the $150 includes about $75 
development/design cost.

So, if anybody wants to do it, let me know..


