With regards to your message at 10:46 AM 2/14/03, Ted Goodridge, Jr. Where 
you stated:
>Would that be guaranteed to fit the LX CPU?
Yes, I have a dead CPU and board here, so I would give it to them for 
fitting purposes.

>Also what type of tube fitting would be used?  (Something like the 
>Innovatek screw fittings?)

Steel nipple, heat pressed into the aluminum.
It is a steel tube, with a ridge/bump around it 1/8" from the end.
1/4" tube slips over it, and most people then use a small tube clamp behind 
the bump to prevent it slipping off.
I could use 3/16" fittings, but that only offers an internal diameter of 
1/8" and I don;t think that is enough cross section for proper flow under 
low pressure.

>If this guy can make it relatively easy to water cool an alpha he may find 
>himself in a nice niche market, with some demand.  If demand is high 
>enough, my not-so-humble opinion is that he would be more than happy to 
>absorb the production/design cost (or divide it among the sales.)

I doubt it. My guess is we *might* sell about 5 pieces..


