In this (so far theoretical) water cooling solution we now have a 
waterblock.  The next hurdle I see is the fan monitoring header on the 
motherboard.  How would one rig a water flow monitor to output correctly to 
that fan header?  The idea being when the flow is correct the fan header 
reads the fan at the proper speed (or even just on?).  When the flow drops 
or is off, the fan header reads the fan as off and shuts down the system.

Any ideas?

Ted




