'linuxconf' is gone for good.  It was always too buggy and full
of nasty surprises.  'gnomecc' is likely still there even if you
do not have an icon for it.

> If they are indeed gone, what are the user-friendly
> replacements, being as they are a little easier to use
> than manually editing config files?

Nautilus is supposed to be able to do everything which 'gnomecc' was
doing (even if its interface is quite horrible your consolation is that
it was designed by "user-friendliness experts").  You should also have
various '*config*' utilities mostly in /usr/bin/ IIRC.

