To minimize the risk of leaks shorting things out, use distilled water.
Distilled water is non conductive.

Many years ago, we used it to cool the anodes on high power tube
amps in a 1 Mw 100KHz transmitter (LORAN, if you know what that is).
The tubes were designed to fit in a water jacket.

