With regards to your message at 11:06 AM 2/14/03, Ted Goodridge, Jr. Where 
you stated:
>In this (so far theoretical) water cooling solution we now have a 
>waterblock.  The next hurdle I see is the fan monitoring header on the 
>motherboard.  How would one rig a water flow monitor to output correctly 
>to that fan header?  The idea being when the flow is correct the fan 
>header reads the fan at the proper speed (or even just on?).  When the 
>flow drops or is off, the fan header reads the fan as off and shuts down 
>the system.
>
>Any ideas?
>
>Ted
Certainly. The motherboard monitors a tach pulse.
A $1.00 piece of TTL can generate that pulse.
But if you want to measure water flow, then we need some fancy, and 
expensive device to measure flow ( these start at around $80 for something 
usable) and then take the signal from it to trigger our production of the 
aforementioned tach pulse.

Lot of work and $$, if you ask me!


