First you need to get to SRM prompt.
Power up the machine and enter CTL-P
several times (control-P is the "official" way
to tell SRM NOT to autoboot using boot flags)
When you see an SRM prompt:

>>>

type 'SHOW DEV'
one of the devices is the CDROM drive
may look like 'DKA0'
put the CD in the drive and type 'BOOT DKA0' and it should boot from CD
one of the devices is the floppy drive
may look like 'DVA0'
can also try 'BOOT DVA0'

You might want to turn OFF autoboot

'SHO AUTO*'
its called AUTO-something
'SET AUTO???=OFF'

to see lots of good stuff try 'SHOW * | MORE'

hope this helps,
Stephen Lewis


