If my memory serves me correctly the problem is that the serial port 
initilization has been changed. One of the mode bits is now set/unset 
where it use to be unset/set in the 2.2 kernels.
If you replace your init also the problem should go away. Mind you I 
think if you change the init then the 2.2 kernels will not work for you. 
Possibly you could install an init.new and use init=/sbin/init.new in 
the boot line to get it to work for you.

