I just installed RH7.2 on a UP2000 that had been running RH7.1,
plus all the updates available through a few days ago, and I
have run into two issues:

  - When I tried to install the kernel-utils RPM, I got the
    following error messages:

error reading information on service microcode_ctl: No such file or directory
error: execution of %post scriptlet from kernel-utils-2.4-8.13.7.2 failed, exit status 1

    I'm not really interested in user-controlled microcode
    updates, if that is what the first line implies, so perhaps
    I don't need this package.

    Is this a known issue?  Should it be filed with HP's bugzilla?

    (I looked in the release notes this time, but I didn't find
    anything about this package.)

  - The mwm window manager seems to have mutated into a very ugly
    thing.  All my menu and function key definitions have quit
    working.  There is this tic-tac-toe board thing called Mwm
    Pager on screen.  When the mouse cursor hits the edge of the
    screen, the screen goes nuts, probably trying to switch to
    another virtual screen.  Also, window border width/color
    definitions have also quit working.

    The man pages don't have anything about how these major
    changes to mwm.

    Does anybody have a pointer to documentation on how to turn
    _OFF_ the pager functions and how to go about restoring menu
    and other functions from .mwmrc that used to work?

    Maybe there's another window manager that works better.  I
    don't want multi-page gunk.  I had been using twm until I
    found that twm refuses to honor program-specified window
    position/placement and insists on placing the windows where
    twm wants them, not where the user wants them.  Does anyone
    know of a clean, non-multi-page window manager that supports
    menus (similar to mwm and twm menus) and allows programs to
    position windows on the screen under program control?

Thanks.

