ATI has 'never' been good at putting proper, unambiguous markings
on their products. Telling the difference between a rage 128
and a 128 pro usually means I have to pull the card, read the markings 
on the ASIC,
and compare it to their oh so helpful list of support drivers (i'm 
talking about windows here).

Comparing different BIOS versions between the same make of card will be 
problematic
at best. Think it's bad now? In two years we'll all be looking for PCI 
matrox G200's and
paying as much for them as a new radeon or close to it. It's because of 
this and other
reasons that I started the console project.

Which BTW is currently at a standstill since I cannot afford the time 
to work on it. So,
if anyone is interested in having modern video cards and boot devices 
(besides IDE) that work
in your Alphas in the very near future you may want to consider jumping 
in.

