I have a suggestion that I think would make it easier to
reliably ensure a RH7.2 system is up to date with the
latest updates.  Being as up2date isn't applicable to the
FTP repository, and being as autorpm sometimes decides a
package (or packages) shouldn't be considered any more, I
would think this would be helpful.

The idea is to include at the FTP site a list of the
package names one would find on a fully updated system
with everything installed.  Ideally, the list would be
sorted alphabetically, but this isn't a big deal.  Then,
we/users/customers could compare this against what we get
from "rpm -qa".

Thanks for considering this idea.

Oh, I installed RH7.2 over the weekend and used autorpm
(plus manual installation of kernel packages), and autorpm
seemed to do the job pretty well.

Robert Riches
