Just another data point,
I have Radeon PCI 7500 working on PWS500
basic system is RedHat 7.1 with locally compiled kernel 2.4.19-pre5
and locally compiled XFree86 4.2.0
card is probed as
"PCI:*(1:9:0) ATI Radeon 7500 QW rev 0"
though I note that the Radeon driver refers to this as an AGP card
"Chipset ATI Radeon 7500 QW (AGP) found"
now as to 2D/3D I am not sure of the definitions
how do you tell if you have "3D"
XFree86 enables DRI and direct rendering - is that "3D" support??
"(II) RADEON(0): Direct rendering enabled"
Maybe I was lucky but I didn't find it particularly difficult
to get this working on Alpha (no worse than getting DRI to work
on a Mac Cube with flat panel :-)
Radeon 7500 PCI is not a bad card under $75 on eBay,

Stephen Lewis

