Upgrading from RH7.1 to RH7.2 has made my HP Scanjet 6300C (CSE?)
connected via USB behave strangely under xsane.  With RH7.1, the
first scan would have to wait for the scanner light to warm up,
and the light would remain on for 10 minutes or so after last
used, so you could do a series of scans fairly quickly.

With RH7.2, the light turns off immediately after each scan, so
each next scan has to wait for the light to warm up.  Also, I'm
getting I/O errors reported at a much higher frequency.  It also
seems that once an I/O error has been reported, that instance of
xsane will never again scan successfully, which requires exiting
xsane and starting up a new xsane process.

Any suggestions?

Thanks.

Robert Riches
rm.riches@verizon.net




