Hello Oliver,

The 7000 works, but the 9000 is a different chipset (R250) and thus a different 3D
driver.  It uses the DRI R200 driver.  To get that support you will have to upgrade
to a 4.3 release candidate for XFree86 and possibly DRI.  Once you do that,
be warned the driver is may not be very stable.  I have a 9000 PCI in a LX164.
It can run glxgears for several minutes standalone.  But if I try to do something
else like display a jpeg at the same time glxgears is running, it locks the box
hard - no serial logon, no ping, no sshd. :-(

On the flip side, 2D on a 9000 is very stable for me.

Alan

