Hi all,
	Am trying to get Redhat 7.2 running on a DEC ALPHA 2100 (A500MP) =
machine.  The machine is fitted with 8 EISA slots and 3 PCI slots.  All =
interface cards (ADPTEC1740 and DAC960 etc) are installed in the EISA =
slots.    I can boot from the installed CDROM drive and every thing =
progresses nicely to the disk partioning stage, at which point I receive =
a 'no devices detected' alert and installation terminates.

	I am reasonably certain the problem lies with the RAID controller cards =
which are MYLEX DAC960LB (P/No D040315-4 and firmware Ver 2.16).

	If any body has any experience on this type of install and can provide =
some pointers to where I am going wrong it would be greatly appreciated.

Thanx

Craig Ryder

