The DAC960 boards that were shipped with the Alpha have DEC BIOS on them 
instead of the manufacturer BIOS.  The linux kernel does not understand the 
DAC960 with the DEC BIOS.  

There is a patch that has been floating about that does not appear to have an 
owner that allows the kernel to recognized the earlier DAC960 boards with DEC 
BIOS.  If you would like to patch the kernel and give it a try, then I would 
be happy to dig about and see if I can find you a copy.

I hope it helps.

Best Regards,


--George

