On Thu, Feb 27, 2003 at 07:43:37PM -0500, Bruce Embrey wrote:
> 
> I have an AlphaServer 800 that has 2 DAC960PD (1 with 2 processors and
> the other has 1).I currently have the firmware version 2.49. If I apply
> the DEC modified update for 2.70/2.73, what will be involve d in getting
> it to be recognized by the install CD or even to be used with 7.2
> version?

First step is to update the firmware; download the docs/fw/utils here:

   http://h18002.www1.hp.com/alphaserver/products/storage/ra230/index.html

and follow the procedure. Then run the RCU to configure the RAID drives
as you desire.

Unfortunately, at the moment, the stock RH 7.2 for Alpha CDs will NOT
function to install to a DAC960-based RAID drive.

As one possible workaround, I suggest the following:

1. install via a SCSI controller to a standard HDD
2. modify (binary edit) the installed DAC960.o module as per previous post
3. "insmod" it, and verify it sees the controllers and RAID drives correctly
4. on destination DAC960 RAID drive, create/edit a BSD partition table,
   making sure to leave space for the bootstrap (~5MB) at the front
5. "swriteboot" the RAID drive, to install aboot
6. (re)build the INITRD image to include the edited DAC960 module
7. "cp -a" the installed system's directories to create an installation
   on the RAID drives' partition(s) from the SCSI HDD
8. edit the new /etc/fstab on the RAID drive to reflect the new root and swap
9. edit the new RAID /etc/aboot.conf to insert the approp. RAID drive device
10. shutdown and boot from the approp. RAID drive

I think that'll do it; I did something very similar, and I think I
remember all the steps. Anyone see something I missed?

Also, I think this is a bit easier than rebuilding the first CD with
all the pertinent DAC960 modules edited, though that would certainly
work and is to be the preferred solution.

Good luck.

 --Jay++

